cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Robust Local Reference Calibration for Open-Set Electrical Fault Diagnosis under Cross-Site Domain Shift"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
type: software
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21904236
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility code for reference-assisted cross-domain open-set electrical
  fault diagnosis using Robust Local Reference (RLR) calibration. The repository
  implements the leakage-free primary evaluation and the reference-duration,
  estimator, contamination, and classifier-family sensitivity studies.
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived Zenodo release and the associated paper."
authors:
  - given-names: Alexandre Giacomelli
    family-names: Leal
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, Brazil
keywords:
  - open-set recognition
  - fault diagnosis
  - domain shift
  - robust local reference
  - electrical monitoring
  - out-of-distribution detection
  - machine learning
repository-code: "https://github.com/Alexandregiacomellileal/rlr-open-set-fault-diagnosis"
